          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A Peek Beyond the Point"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.088,
            0.416,
            0.342
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can say that its length is between "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "^ { 4 } \\mathrm { ~ \\frac { ~ 4 ~ } { ~ 1 0 ~ } ~ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " units and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 ~ { \\frac { 5 } { 1 0 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " units. But we cannot state its exact measurement, since there are no markings. Earlier, we split a unit into 10 one-tenths to measure smaller lengths. We can do something similar and split each one-tenth into 10 parts."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.358,
            0.415,
            0.437
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the length of this smaller part? How many such smaller parts make a unit length?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.437,
            0.102,
            0.857,
            0.437
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.437,
                0.102,
                0.857,
                0.437
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_7_image_3.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.446,
            0.416,
            0.484
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As shown in the figure below, each one-tenth has"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.483,
            0.848,
            0.557
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10 smaller parts, and there are 10 one-tenths in a unit; therefore, there will be 100 smaller parts in a unit. Therefore, one part’s length will be "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 1 0 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of a unit."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.228,
            0.572,
            0.767,
            0.707
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.228,
                0.572,
                0.767,
                0.707
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_7_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.742,
            0.848,
            0.819
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Returning to our question, what is the length of the folded paper? We can see that it ends at "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4   { \\frac { 4 } { 1 0 } } { \\frac { 5 } { 1 0 0 } } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " read as 4 units and 4 one-tenths and 5 one-hundredths."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.838,
            0.803,
            0.88
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How many one-hundredths make one-tenth? Can we also say that the length is 4 units and 45 one-hundredths?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
